    {
      "id": "e222",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1130,
      "y": 1398,
      "width": 753.3077178306454,
      "height": 30,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786303843718,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Install at least two spare conduits on any path you cannot reopen cheaply - between floors, through\nrated construction, and to the entrance facility. Both are nearly free now.",
      "originalText": "1. Install at least two spare conduits on any path you cannot reopen cheaply - between floors, through rated construction, and to the entrance facility. Both are nearly free now.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 218,
      "versionNonce": 1042545236,
      "index": "b2Z",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e223",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1130,
      "y": 1448,
      "width": 756.1314698799652,
      "height": 30,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786303851245,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. Conduit is not the telecom bonding system. Bond it, and run the TBB and rack bonding conductors\nseparately - see E-302.",
      "originalText": "2. Conduit is not the telecom bonding system. Bond it, and run the TBB and rack bonding conductors separately - see E-302.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 196,
      "versionNonce": 831585388,
      "index": "b2a",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e224",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1130,
      "y": 1483,
      "width": 735.424471880285,
      "height": 30,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786303854597,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Never terminate a conduit directly over a rack without a drip loop, and never route condensate or any\nwet service above one - see M-302.",
      "originalText": "3. Never terminate a conduit directly over a rack without a drip loop, and never route condensate or any wet service above one - see M-302.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 83,
      "versionNonce": 430146388,
      "index": "b2b",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e225",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1130,
      "y": 1518,
      "width": 735.8952264790046,
      "height": 15,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786303859205,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. Use innerduct where fiber shares a conduit with anything else, so the next pull cannot chafe it.",
      "originalText": "4. Use innerduct where fiber shares a conduit with anything else, so the next pull cannot chafe it.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
